[thin] These exact opposite surfaces bound the 0.75 mm roof over a 6.30 mm diameter, 2.25 mm deep storage socket in the 3.00 mm heel. It is a local docking roof, not the active angle or support-ceiling comparison. The socket is open from the bed side and the prepared project records the actual support/bridge treatment; the nominal thickness is not a strength or lifetime claim.
alternatives: Thickening this roof to 3.00 mm requires a 5.25 mm heel with the same socket depth, adding 2.25 mm and changing the heel/display datum. Opening the socket through the heel removes the roof but perforates the upper sample face. Shorter pegs reduce socket depth and leave more roof, with less storage engagement.
