[thin] These shortest approaches are around the common 24 by 7 by 3 mm identifier pad above the cantilever, toward its rounded edge or the start of the raised identifier. The pad is backed by the full roof and upright; the readings are not the 3.00 mm active cantilever thickness. The larger roof-thickness reading is answered separately.
alternatives: A wider or square-edged identifier pad increases these local corner distances but adds material/cooling area above the comparison roof. Making the entire upper region uniformly thicker also changes roof rigidity and thermal exposure. Moving the identifier to a separate tag removes this pad but introduces a detachable identity that can be mismatched.
